+# kv-stream-brick scripts
+
+Scripts behind brick's measurements (GTX 1650 Max-Q 4 GB, i7-9750H, Qwen3.5 4B Q4_K_M). They expect a work folder
+($KV_STREAM_BRICK, default ~/code/kv-stream-brick) holding this clone as llama.cpp-adaptive-kv-streaming (built in
+build-sm75 by build.sh), the model in models/, and runs/, slots/ and results/ for output.
+
+- build.sh: the sm_75 build (configure with -DGGML_CUDA_KV_STREAM_D512=OFF).
+- longctx.py: exact-length prompts from the fork's .md files (split sweeps).
+- split-smoke.sh: one server run with or without LLAMA_KV_SPLIT; LLAMA_KV_SPLIT_VERIFY=1 compares every decode layer
+  with CPU attention over the whole context.
+- split-sweep.sh: reads a prompt once, saves the slot, then restores it for each split setting.
+- measure.sh: the release set (plain, spill 1, spill 2, stream, split, stream at 250K). It runs probe-longctx.py,
+  copied to $KV_STREAM_BRICK/probe/longctx.py, with PROBE_SRC pointing at a `git archive` of this fork's src, common
+  and tools/server at bcf1a81d6.
+- fa-cpu.cpp: standalone CPU flash attention benchmark in the split's shape. Build:
+  g++ -O2 -std=c++17 -Iggml/include -Iggml/src fa-cpu.cpp -Lbuild-sm75/bin -lggml -lggml-base -lggml-cpu
+
+Split attention environment: LLAMA_KV_SPLIT=auto or a fraction in (0, 1); LLAMA_KV_SPLIT_THREADS (default two thirds
+of the hardware threads); LLAMA_KV_SPLIT_DEBUG; LLAMA_KV_SPLIT_VERIFY; LLAMA_KV_SPLIT_NOOP (measuring only, output
+wrong).
